text:
alex: FYI onboarding sample app failing on customer CI. They bundle our JS SDK into an ESM lib and deploy to Vercel Edge. Errors: double POSTs to token endpoint + "body used" exceptions. Happens only when they build with esbuild + node targets. anyone seen this? :grimacing:

nina: seen variants. main culprits: (a) two different fetch impls end up in the bundle (global + undici polyfill), (b) differences in body cloning semantics between runtimes, (c) our auth refresh currently triggers a retry path that reuses the original Request object.

rachel: bundlers matter. if package.exports or types/entry points aren't explicit, some bundlers will resolve the CJS entry which imports undici. that forces undici into ESM edge bundles. double-check "exports" map and add an explicit small ESM entry that does runtime detection only.

tom: concrete runtime-detect snippet i've used: 
```js
export function resolveFetch() {
  if (typeof globalThis.fetch === 'function') return globalThis.fetch;
  // only import undici when running in Node without global fetch
  return import('undici').then(m => m.fetch);
}
```
Make sure this file is pure ESM and small so tree-shaking doesn't pull undici into browser/edge builds.

alex: good. what about the retry/auth logic? customers are seeing duplicate non-idempotent requests.

nina: two safe changes: (1) single-flight refresh so only one refresh request at a time, (2) a replay-safety check before retrying. for replay-safety: treat strings/objects/buffers as safe; treat ReadableStream/FormData/File/Blob as unsafe unless explicitly buffered.

rachel: also add a small opt-in buffer policy: buffer up to X bytes (e.g., 64KB) for non-idempotent calls if consumer sets "allowReplaySmallBodies: true". default off. that lets uploads with small payloads retry without surprising everyone.

tom: code sketch: 
```js
function isReplayableBody(body) {
  if (!body) return true;
  if (typeof body === 'string') return true;
  if (Buffer && Buffer.isBuffer(body)) return true;
  // plain objects -> JSON stringify -> safe
  if (Object.prototype.toString.call(body) === '[object Object]') return true;
  // streams/files are not replayable by default
  return false;
}
```

alex: typings are another pain. TS users on Node 18/20 with ESM sometimes don't have DOM libs. we should publish our own small types to avoid forcing lib.dom on consumers.

rachel: suggestion: include an index.d.ts that re-exports a minimal Fetch type alias and declare a global augmentation file consumers can opt-into. also add "typesVersions" in package.json to point ESM -> types/esm.d.ts so editors pick correct shapes.

tom: also add package.json hints to avoid bundling undici: 
- "exports" with explicit "import" path for ESM
- mark undici as optionalPeerDependency or peerDependency and set peerDependenciesMeta.undici.optional = true
- recommend bundlers external: ['undici'] for rollup/esbuild

rachel: example exports map: 
```json
"exports": {
  "./package.json": "./package.json",
  "./": {
    "import": "./dist/esm/index.js",
    "require": "./dist/cjs/index.js",
    "default": "./dist/esm/index.js"
  }
}
```
and add "sideEffects": false to help tree-shakers.

alex: we should also add a CI matrix that builds our sample app for: ESM+Vercel Edge, ESM+Cloudflare, CJS+Node 18/20 and run integration tests that simulate token expiry and non-replayable bodies.

ci-bot: created ticket SDK-5721 and scheduled nightly matrix job: https://redwood/tasks/SDK-5721. results will post to #devex with a short failure summary.

nina: small docs note: explicitly call out "do not bundle undici into edge builds" and show esbuild/rollup externals. include a reproducer that demonstrates a token refresh race resulting in duplicate POSTs.

rachel: i'll prepare a tiny PR that: (1) adds runtime fetch resolver, (2) updates exports, (3) adds isReplayable heuristics, (4) includes types shim. keeping changes internal-only and feature-flag guarded.

tom: tests i'll add: token singleflight concurrency test, non-replayable-body rejects retry test, small-buffer replay allowed test, and a bundler smoke test ensuring undici isn't present in the edge bundle.

alex: thanks. once PR lands, let's update onboarding sample and CI to run the reproducer so we catch regressions in future.
